WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.753 --> 00:00:05.464
In the world of See,
you can be the queen,

00:00:05.756 --> 00:00:07.549
you can be a leader of a tribe,

00:00:07.799 --> 00:00:08.884
you can be a warrior.

00:00:08.884 --> 00:00:11.553
Each individual is
treated as an equal in our show.

00:00:15.057 --> 00:00:16.266
I gotta do something as an actor

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:17.142
that i’ve never done before.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:19.770
I’ve worked so hard to
play a character like this.

00:00:20.354 --> 00:00:22.397
It was just incredible
to work with Joe.

00:00:23.065 --> 00:00:24.650
He’s a producer and he’s blind.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:28.028
And he’s there to further
the development of the

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:30.197
characters in the
best way possible.

00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:32.157
Heres Joe Strechay to
give you some more advice.

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:34.326
It’s beautiful to have
someone like Joe

00:00:34.326 --> 00:00:34.952
to help me through it.

00:00:35.494 --> 00:00:37.537
We wanted to make sure
we were representing

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.122
our community positively.

00:00:39.957 --> 00:00:42.793
So we looked at
the littlest behaviors

00:00:42.793 --> 00:00:45.671
and how characters who
are blind move in the world.

00:00:46.797 --> 00:00:48.507
I went in completely openminded.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:49.591
And Joe will come up

00:00:49.591 --> 00:00:50.968
and give me his notes
and I’ll say,

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:52.719
“I just never even
 thought about it that way.”

00:00:53.136 --> 00:00:54.721
We tried to do everything we can

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.765
to make sure that
this feels authentic

00:00:56.765 --> 00:00:59.601
for the blind community
and Joe is key in that.

00:01:00.519 --> 00:01:03.146
We have numerous actors who
are blind or low vision

00:01:03.522 --> 00:01:05.148
and we want to make
sure that their needs

00:01:05.148 --> 00:01:06.316
are met when they come to work.

00:01:06.942 --> 00:01:07.651
This was amazing.

00:01:07.651 --> 00:01:08.610
It was just such an experience.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:09.778
I was treated

00:01:09.778 --> 00:01:11.780
just with the
utmost care and respect.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.157
Everyone has such
a good relationship,

00:01:14.157 --> 00:01:15.575
and here, everyone’s like,

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.494
“you’re an actor,
you’re with us.”

00:01:17.536 --> 00:01:20.664
We fight for our families!
We fight for our freedom!

00:01:20.664 --> 00:01:21.665
[Cheers]

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.209
We try to make sure

00:01:24.209 --> 00:01:25.836
that our characters,
who are blind,

00:01:25.836 --> 00:01:28.088
aren’t using
non-verbal communication.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:30.215
You know, like,
even nodding the head yes

00:01:30.215 --> 00:01:31.675
or shaking the head no.

00:01:32.301 --> 00:01:34.594
We’re gonna use our
ears to listen, right?

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:36.430
We’re not looking at him speak,

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:38.140
we’re listening to
him speak, right?

00:01:38.515 --> 00:01:41.143
Physical gestures mean
very little in this world.

00:01:42.311 --> 00:01:43.312
If you’re moving your hands,

00:01:43.312 --> 00:01:44.938
it should be purposeful around

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:47.441
grabbing something,
touching something,

00:01:49.026 --> 00:01:51.278
making a sound with your hands.

00:01:51.278 --> 00:01:52.279
[Bells Ring]

00:01:53.238 --> 00:01:55.907
They’ve done such a
great job in the way

00:01:55.907 --> 00:01:58.744
they portray blindness
or visual impairments.

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:00.579
Joe started to teach me

00:02:00.579 --> 00:02:01.955
about echo location.

00:02:03.707 --> 00:02:04.541
You make sound.

00:02:04.708 --> 00:02:05.834
[Clicks]

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:07.419
♪♪

00:02:08.003 --> 00:02:10.088
And then, find out
the size of a room.

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:12.883
Beautiful room.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.134
Where people are.

00:02:14.509 --> 00:02:17.262
I had no idea that was
something that people could do.

00:02:18.847 --> 00:02:21.433
Everything is inceptionally
designed to be

00:02:21.433 --> 00:02:22.351
authentic to what

00:02:22.351 --> 00:02:23.352
in a world would be like,

00:02:23.352 --> 00:02:25.437
if most of the world
didn’t have sight.

00:02:26.188 --> 00:02:27.522
The things we
built are beautiful,

00:02:27.522 --> 00:02:29.441
but there also a lot
of logic built in.

00:02:30.233 --> 00:02:32.110
Like putting tap lines down
the middle of the road

00:02:32.444 --> 00:02:34.154
to get their direction
so they find a path.

00:02:34.571 --> 00:02:37.157
The plates had individual little
grooves around the edge

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:39.451
of the chargers so that
the staff can acualy

00:02:39.451 --> 00:02:41.411
figure out where
the table setting is

00:02:41.787 --> 00:02:43.789
in the wedding the ribbon
hadbells on them so that

00:02:43.789 --> 00:02:45.415
everyone could here
the reaction.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.627
[Cheers]

00:02:49.586 --> 00:02:50.295
With wardrobe

00:02:50.295 --> 00:02:52.506
it forces you to use your other
sences for fabrics,

00:02:52.506 --> 00:02:53.799
for touches, for texture

00:02:53.799 --> 00:02:55.842
and then also
does it make sound.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.263
I was really proud of everyone.

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:01.932
How hard everyone trained.

00:03:03.266 --> 00:03:04.851
We work with every performer

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:06.478
to help bring them in
the world of See.

00:03:07.562 --> 00:03:10.190
And then the team really
creates something beautiful.

